# Game_Memory — Matching Pairs (ID 19)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_Memory.h, Game_Memory.cpp
# HTML: data/game_memory_setup.html, game_memory_names.html, game_memory_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Classic memory/concentration. Pucks have hidden colors in pairs. Reveal two per turn.
Match → stay revealed. Mismatch → hide again. Find all pairs to win.

## CONFIG
- numPucks (4-MAX_PEERS, must be even)
- memorizeTime: 0=2s, 1=5s, 2=10s
- autoRestart, searchMode (rainbow instead of initial reveal)

## STATES
MEM_SETUP → MEM_MEMORIZE (show colors) or MEM_SEARCH_INIT (3s rainbow) → MEM_RUNNING → MEM_EVALUATE (1.5s) → loop → MEM_FINISHED (4s rainbow) → MEM_IDLE

## KEY MECHANICS
- Fisher-Yates shuffle for color randomization
- 10-color PALETTE, each used exactly twice
- First click: reveal puck color
- Second click: check match
  - Match: pairsFound++, both stay off (solved), DINGDONG
  - Mismatch: errors++, red fail, ERROR sequence, hide both
- Reveal command: trainer can expose all unsolved for 2s
- MEM_REVEAL state: 2s showing unsolved colors
- Odd puck count auto-decreased by 1

## COMMANDS
setup, cfg_pucks, cfg_speed, cfg_auto, cfg_search, start, stop, reset, reveal, exit

## STATUS JSON
{st, pf (pairs found), err (errors), tot (total pairs)}
